---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { href } from "../data/site";
---
<Base title="Governance" description="How the ORCHESTRA handles data, licences, provenance and refusal: data classes, the GRDC firewall, per-package licences, the Independent Oracle Principle and the typed decline." path="/governance">
  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="kicker">Governance</p>
      <h1>Data, licences, provenance, refusal</h1>
      <p class="prose lead mt-2">Four rules make the orchestra's outputs safe to act on and safe to share.
        They are stated here so a research manager, a data custodian or a reviewer can check them without
        reading code.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2 class="mt-3">Data classes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Public.</strong> Published trial datasets, public climate and soil services, simulators.
          The only class that appears in package examples, tests and vignettes.</li>
        <li><strong>Synthetic with a known truth.</strong> Generated belts and multi-environment trials whose
          truth is planted, so a method can be graded on recovery. Every study in the series runs on one.</li>
        <li><strong>Sovereign twin.</strong> A structurally faithful synthetic clone of a real dataset,
          produced by the owner with masque. Analysis is developed on the clone and replayed on the real
          rows by the custodian; only aggregates leave. No real row enters a package, a page or a poster.</li>
        <li><strong>Restricted.</strong> Ethics-restricted or contract-restricted data. Never enters the
          orchestra's packages, tests, sites or publications, in any form.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="mt-3">The GRDC firewall</h2>
      <p class="mt-1">No GRDC-origin code or data enters any orchestra package, study artefact or public
        surface. Where a GRDC-approved dataset is used for research, it is used only through the sovereign-twin
        route, aggregates only, and any publication of those aggregates is gated on the GRDC manager's
        agreement. The orchestra is generic on purpose: that is what lets a GRDC pipeline consume it downstream.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-3">Licences and channels</h2>
      <p class="mt-1">Members are open source under MIT or GPL, per package, and are published or staged under
        <code>max578</code> with an R-universe channel. An AAGI-AUS mirror of this site and of the member
        packages is prepared but not declared: no licence is chosen for the mirror until the licence
        conversation with the GRDC manager has happened among all interested parties.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-3">Provenance</h2>
      <p class="mt-1">Every inference result is an <code>orchestra_manifest</code>: emitter, version,
        inferential target, parameter draws, outputs, a hash over the payload, and the lineage of the manifests
        it consumed. A tampered manifest fails verification, a derived manifest without lineage is rejected,
        and a report generated from manifests can bind every printed number to the object it came from.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-3">The Independent Oracle Principle</h2>
      <p class="mt-1">A fact about an external authority — a service's response shape, a dataset's columns, a
        constant, a citation — is checked against a reference the orchestra did not itself produce. A test whose
        expected value shares the claim's source proves self-consistency, not correspondence to reality.
        Un-grounded facts are marked <em>unverified</em> and a decision layer refuses to price them: this is how a
        crop-model posterior the field has rejected never becomes a nitrogen rate.</p>

      <h2 class="mt-3">The typed decline</h2>
      <p class="mt-1">A refusal or an abstention is an object, not an error message. Every member can emit one,
        every consumer can recognise one with a single predicate, and a fleet gate exercises one real trigger
        per member. A decision taken over a decline is a contract violation, and the decision layer does not
        take it.</p>

      <p class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={href("/a0")}>Study A0 results</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={href("/about")}>About</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
